---
layout: layouts/base.njk
tape: true
title: Sarthak Bichhawa — Sr. Data & Applied Scientist · Microsoft
desc: "The case for hiring Sarthak Bichhawa: nine years of production ML and AI — autonomous multi-agent LLM systems, a fleet-scale embedding platform, and revenue-critical data systems. Claims up front, receipts attached."
---

<!-- ============================================================
     HERO — the claim
     ============================================================ -->
<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="hero-no"><span class="no">Passionate about data.</span></p>
      <h1>The case for<br>hiring <em>Sarthak.</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">{{ facts.summary.hero }}</p>
      <p class="hero-meta">
        <b class="seg">{{ facts.identity.title }}</b> <span class="sep">·</span> <span class="seg">{{ facts.identity.org }}, {{ facts.identity.team }}</span>
        <span class="sep">·</span> <span class="seg">since {{ facts.identity.tenure_start }}</span> <span class="sep">·</span> <span class="seg">{{ facts.identity.location }}</span><br>
        <span class="open">OPEN TO: {{ facts.identity.open_to | join(" · ") }}</span>
      </p>
      <div class="hero-ctas">
        <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="hero-email">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg>
          Email me
        </a>
        <a href="/resume/" class="text-link" data-goatcounter-click="hero-resume">Résumé →</a>
        <button class="btn btn-mono copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="hero-copy-summary">⧉ copy candidate summary</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- reader lanes -->
    <div class="lanes panel reveal">
      <div class="lanes-head">
        <span>Reader lanes — pick your depth</span>
        <span class="lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      </div>
      <div class="lanes-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Reader lanes">
        <button role="tab" id="tab-recruiter" aria-controls="lane-recruiter" aria-selected="true">recruiter · 30s</button>
        <button role="tab" id="tab-hm" aria-controls="lane-hm" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">hiring mgr · 5 min</button>
        <button role="tab" id="tab-eng" aria-controls="lane-eng" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">engineer · deep</button>
      </div>
      <div class="lanes-body">
        <div class="lane" id="lane-recruiter" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-recruiter">
          <p class="lane-label">Recruiter · 30 seconds</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Level &amp; track:</strong> senior IC at {{ facts.identity.org }} ({{ facts.identity.team }}), {{ facts.identity.years }} yrs total — targeting {{ facts.identity.open_to | join(" · ") }}.</li>
            <li><strong>Location:</strong> {{ facts.identity.location }} · <a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn profile</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Fastest path:</strong> grab the <a href="/resume/">résumé</a>, or copy a paste-ready summary for your ATS / intro email.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="lane-actions">
            <a href="/resume/" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="lane-resume">Résumé</a>
            <button class="btn btn-mono copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="lane-copy-summary">⧉ copy summary</button>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lane" id="lane-hm" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-hm" hidden>
          <p class="lane-label">Hiring manager · 5 minutes</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>What you get:</strong> someone who ships agents with evals <em>before</em> demos, builds platforms other teams adopt, and holds the room at GM / CVP readouts.</li>
            <li><strong>How he decides:</strong> five <a href="#judgment">judgment calls</a> below — each with the trade-off, the outcome, and the question to grill him on.</li>
            <li><strong>Scope signals:</strong> led 4 DS + 2 interns at Walmart Labs · 8+ teams aligned on one program · 4-team cross-org Sev2 command.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="lane-actions">
            <a href="#receipts" class="btn btn-primary">Start with the receipts</a>
            <a href="/case/incident-agent/" class="btn btn-ghost">Exhibit A</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lane" id="lane-eng" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="tab-eng" hidden>
          <p class="lane-label">Engineer · go deep</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Agent internals:</strong> hand-rolled planner / executor on Azure OpenAI — no LangChain — 10 MCP tools, concurrent dispatch, self-compacting 200K context, full LLM tracing.</li>
            <li><strong>ML internals:</strong> unsupervised autoencoder + FAISS over ~100 behavioral features per account, pooled hierarchically account → subscription → customer.</li>
            <li><strong>Receipts in code:</strong> the <a href="/case/incident-agent/">incident-agent case file</a> carries the run trace, confidence rubric, and eval table.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="lane-actions">
            <a href="/case/incident-agent/" class="btn btn-primary">Read the run trace</a>
            <a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost">GitHub</a>
            <a href="/writing/" class="btn btn-ghost">Field notes</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- the headline receipts -->
    <div class="reveal" id="receipts">
      <div class="receipts panel">
        {%- for r in facts.receipts %}
        <a class="receipt" href="{{ r.anchor }}">
          <span class="r-ref">receipt → {{ r.anchor }}</span>
          <span class="r-val">{{ r.value }}</span>
          <span class="r-lbl">{{ r.label }}</span>
          <span class="r-sub">{{ r.sub }}</span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
      <p class="mono-note strip-note">// every number on this page links to its receipt. <span class="g">click through.</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<!-- ============================================================
     §01 — SYSTEMS LEDGER
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="ledger" style="padding-top:3.25rem;">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§01 — Systems on the record</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">What runs in production, with proof.</h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Not prototypes, not weekend demos — systems running inside Microsoft Azure Storage with users, on-call rotations, and numbers attached.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="board panel reveal">
      <div class="board-head">
        <span>ID</span><span>System</span><span>What it does</span><span>Proof</span><span>Status</span>
      </div>
      {%- for row in facts.systems %}
      <div class="board-row">
        <span class="b-id">{{ row.id }}</span>
        <span class="b-name"><a href="{{ row.link }}">{{ row.name }}</a></span>
        <span class="b-desc">{{ row.what }}</span>
        <span class="b-proof">{{ row.proof }}</span>
        <span class="b-status {{ 'live' if row.status == 'LIVE' else 'prod' }}"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ row.status }}</span>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
      <div class="board-foot">// side projects don't get a row. <span class="g">everything above ran in production with users who could file incidents.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §02 — THE EXHIBITS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="exhibits">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§02 — The exhibits</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title flip">The work, <em>architecture attached.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Each exhibit opens into a full case file — planner design, prompts, eval output, the parts a hiring loop actually wants to inspect.
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- for c in facts.cases %}
    <article class="exhibit" id="{{ c.id }}">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="exhibit-tag">{{ c.tag }}</div>
        <h3 class="case-title">{{ c.title }}</h3>
        <p class="case-lede">{{ c.tease }}</p>
      </div>
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-incident" %}{% include "partials/diagram-incident.njk" %}{% endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-mcc" %}{% include "partials/diagram-mcc.njk" %}{% endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-a2v" %}{% include "partials/diagram-a2v.njk" %}{% endif %}
      {%- if c.id == "exhibit-stress" %}
      <div class="metric-row panel reveal">
        <div class="m"><span class="v">20</span><span class="d">workload types stress-tested per build</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">~500</span><span class="d">failure signals distilled</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">15</span><span class="d">recurring failure modes named</span></div>
        <div class="m"><span class="v">−60%</span><span class="d">false positives after bandit-tuned scoring</span></div>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      <a href="{{ c.slug }}" class="case-cta panel reveal">
        <span>{{ c.scent }}</span>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
      </a>
    </article>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §03 — JUDGMENT CALLS
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="judgment">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§03 — Judgment</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Five calls I'd defend <em>in the interview.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Senior hires aren't judged on tools — they're judged on decisions under ambiguity. Here are five of mine, with the trade-off and the outcome. Each comes with the question you should grill me on.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="calls-grid">
      <article class="call panel reveal">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 01</span><span class="dom">architecture</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[0].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The incident agent started on LangChain / LangGraph. Debugging through five layers of someone else's abstraction was slower than owning the loop — so I <strong>replaced it with a hand-rolled planner / executor</strong>: full LLM tracing to Kusto, 429-storm retry, context compaction we control, concurrent tool dispatch.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ faster iteration, traceable failures, an agent on-call actually trusts</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[0].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call panel reveal">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 02</span><span class="dom">quality</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[1].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The MCC copilot didn't meet a single real user until a <strong>golden-set eval harness, guardrails, and PII-aware prompts</strong> existed. Demos earn applause; evals earn production. The harness now gates every prompt and model change like CI.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ 8+ teams on one surface, leadership quoting its numbers unprompted</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[1].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call panel reveal">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 03</span><span class="dom">platform</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[2].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          Account2Vec could have shipped as one team's similarity model. Instead I <strong>named the abstraction, wrote the design doc, and built the drift / coverage / staleness plumbing</strong> that makes other teams safe to depend on it — account, subscription, and customer tiers included.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ 5+ downstream consumers building on one representation</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[2].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call panel reveal">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 04</span><span class="dom">trust</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[3].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          Revenue data is only useful if Finance can't break it. I rebuilt partner attribution to <strong>&lt;1% variance vs. Finance</strong> (~$45M/mo, ~4× coverage), then shipped the data-quality service — 76 tests, 4 security gates — that <strong>caught an ~88% upstream row collapse</strong> before a single dashboard went wrong.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ GM / CVP-level reliance; PMs accept the dashboards as governed source</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[3].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>

      <article class="call call-wide panel reveal">
        <div class="call-kicker"><span>Call 05</span><span class="dom">experimentation</span></div>
        <h3 class="call-title">{{ facts.judgment[4].title }}.</h3>
        <p class="call-body">
          The pre-release stress lab ran thousands of simulations per build across <strong>20 workload types</strong>, throwing off ~500 failure signals — far more than a static test plan could triage. The roadmap argued for coverage; the data argued for yield — so I <strong>put multi-armed bandits in charge of picking the next scenario</strong> and tuned scoring thresholds on outcomes, cutting false positives 60%. The program came to inform per-build ship / hold calls and helped prevent 10+ Sev1/Sev2 incidents; I led the 2-person effort and wrote the design doc and internal white paper.
        </p>
        <p class="call-out">→ per-build ship / hold calls; 10+ Sev1/Sev2 incidents prevented before rollout</p>
        <p class="call-ask"><b>ASK ME ABOUT:</b> {{ facts.judgment[4].ask_me_about }}</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §04 — THE RECORD
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="record">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§04 — The record</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Nine years of ML that had to <em>earn its keep.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Mu Sigma → IAS → Walmart Labs → Microsoft. The thread: turn ambiguity into a system, then verify the system actually moved the number it claimed it would.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel ledger-wrap reveal">
      <div class="lt-head">Career ledger — one row per era, one number each</div>
      <table class="ledger-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Years</th><th scope="col">Role / system</th><th scope="col">One number</th><th scope="col"><span aria-hidden="true">§</span><span class="sr-only">Reference</span></th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- for row in facts.career_ledger %}
          <tr>
            <td class="lt-years">{{ row.years }}</td>
            <td class="lt-role">{{ row.role }}</td>
            <td class="lt-num">{{ row.number }}</td>
            <td class="lt-ref"><a href="{{ row.ref }}" aria-label="Jump to {{ row.role }}">§</a></td>
          </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-list">
      {%- for r in facts.record %}
      <article class="rec panel reveal{{ ' rec-compact' if not r.workstreams }}" id="{{ r.id }}">
        <div class="rec-head">
          <h3 class="rec-role">{{ r.role }}</h3>
          <span class="rec-co">{{ r.company }} · {{ r.location }}</span>
          <span class="rec-dates">{{ r.dates }}</span>
        </div>
        {%- if r.leadership_band %}
        <div class="rec-band">
          <span class="band-k">Leadership band</span>
          <ul>
            {%- for item in r.leadership_band %}<li>{{ item }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if r.workstreams %}
        {%- for ws in r.workstreams %}
        <div class="rec-ws">
          <h4>{{ ws.name }}</h4>
          <ul class="rec-points">
            {%- for b in ws.bullets %}<li>{{ b }}</li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- else %}
        <ul class="rec-points">
          {%- for b in r.bullets %}<li>{{ b }}</li>{% endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <p class="edu-line">
      {%- for e in facts.education %}<b>{{ e.degree }}</b> — {{ e.school }} ({{ e.dates }}){% if not loop.last %}<span class="sep">·</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </p>

    <div class="skills-table panel reveal">
      <div class="skills-row"><span class="k">AI / ML</span><span class="v">{{ facts.skills.ai_ml }}</span></div>
      <div class="skills-row"><span class="k">Tools</span><span class="v">{{ facts.skills.tools }}</span></div>
      <div class="skills-row"><span class="k">Platforms</span><span class="v">{{ facts.skills.platforms }}</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<hr class="rule"/>

<!-- ============================================================
     §05 — FIELD NOTES
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="section-pad" id="writing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§05 — Field notes</div>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Notes from production, <em>where the demos go to die.</em></h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        The gap between the prototype that wows a leadership review and the system that survives real engineers trying to break it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="writing-list">
      {%- for w in facts.writing %}
      {%- if w.url %}
      <a href="{{ w.url }}" class="write-row panel reveal">
        <div class="write-when">{{ w.date | humanDate }}</div>
        <div class="write-title">{{ w.title }}</div>
        <span class="write-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19"/></svg>
        </span>
      </a>
      {%- else %}
      <div class="write-row pending panel reveal">
        <div class="write-when">in queue</div>
        <div class="write-title">{{ w.title }}</div>
        <span class="write-status">{{ w.status }}</span>
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================
     §06 — THE ASK
     ============================================================ -->
<section class="ask" id="ask">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="sec-mark">§06 — The ask</div>
      <h2 class="ask-title">The evidence rests.<br><em>Your move.</em></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="ask-person reveal">
      <img class="ask-photo" src="/assets/sarthak.jpg" alt="Sarthak Bichhawa" width="116" height="116" loading="lazy" />
      <p>
        Hi, I'm <strong>Sarthak</strong>. I lead the design and delivery of the systems this page just walked you through — the agents, the embeddings, the attribution layers Finance reconciles against.
        I'm drawn to problems where the data is ambiguous and the stakes are real, and nine years in the thread is consistent: turn ambiguity into a system, then verify it moved the number it claimed it would.
        Hiring for a <strong>{{ facts.identity.open_to | join(", ") }}</strong>? Email me — I respond fast, and I'll bring the architecture diagrams.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="ask-ctas reveal">
      <a href="mailto:{{ facts.identity.email }}" class="btn btn-primary" data-goatcounter-click="ask-email">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6"/></svg>
        {{ facts.identity.email }}
      </a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="ask-linkedin">LinkedIn</a>
      <a href="{{ facts.identity.github }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-ghost" data-goatcounter-click="ask-github">GitHub</a>
      <button class="btn btn-mono copy-btn" type="button" data-goatcounter-click="ask-copy-summary">⧉ copy candidate summary</button>
    </div>

    <div class="resume-dossier panel reveal">
      <div class="rd-head">The résumé dossier — three documents, one story</div>
      <div class="rd-list">
        {%- for r in facts.resumes %}
        <a href="{{ r.file }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-goatcounter-click="resume-{{ loop.index }}">
          <b>{{ r.label }}</b><span class="rd-note">{{ r.note }}</span>
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="text/plain" id="ats-summary">{{ facts.summary.ats | safe }}
Site: {{ facts.meta.site_url }} · Résumé: {{ facts.meta.site_url }}/resumes/SarthakBichhawa_Resume_2026.pdf · LinkedIn: {{ facts.identity.linkedin }} · Email: {{ facts.identity.email }}</script>
